the vikings had a different dynamic in  the division around they had had a  hard-fought win unexpectedly in the wild  card round of the playoffs and that  wasn't enough to carry them over the top  they lost 27-10 to the san francisco  49ers now they have some decisions to  make some big decisions to make it looks  like mike zimmer is going to remain as  the head coach peter but he's entering  the final year of his contract here he  is at his end of season press conference  addressing his expectation that talks  aimed at extending his deal will begin  in the not too distant future  like i said a couple weeks ago was  talking about this  i love these players this organization  you know the owners have been  outstanding to me  so  uh i believe that there'll be  conversations here in in the near future  and uh whatever happens  i'm happy with it  i mean look the bottom line is you  either have to pay the guy or move on  from him i don't like the idea of  letting him coach his lame duck season  although it's happened frequently it is  a distraction as we saw or it can be a  distraction as we saw this year with  jason garrett in dallas it constantly  comes up what are you going to do what  are you going to do what are you going  to do i think the vikings know at this  point whether they want to keep mike  zimmer or not and the indications are  they'll find a way to try to extend his  deal but peter of the guys who have one  year left on their contracts gm rick  spielman head coach mike zimmer  quarterback kirk cousins running back  dalvin cook who would you make your top  priority in locking up beyond this  coming season  i'm tempted to say cousins but i think i  would rather say  mike zimmer  and i think the zimmer thing is going to  be difficult mike  just because mike zimmer's a competitive  guy  and i think every coach that has to  re-sign now who's had success mike  zimmer has this team as a contender  every year now obviously they haven't  gotten they haven't even sniffed a super  bowl you know or been close but  they have been a contender  every july when they come to training  camp so now you say my if i were mike  zimmer's agent my first  uh  my first shot out of the box to mark and  ziggy wilf would be  let's talk about matt rules contract  all right  and let's just start this thing at 8.7  million  uh a year  and and by the way we're not signing for  8.7 million a year you know let's talk  about a fair contract for a guy who's  had this team in contention  at the end of every season he's coached  virtually and so i think it's going to  be difficult i think the cousin's  contract is going to be exceedingly hard  just because  are you going to ask kirk cousins to  take a pay cut  uh probably not and now you have to ask  yourself  do you want to sign kirk cousins for the  sort of the near future  at 30 million dollars a year that's  that's one of the questions like i think  a lot of vikings fans would say even  though we know that uh he's not the best  quarterback in the league we need a  quarterback and we don't want to start  from ground zero so i think a lot of  people would say you just got to pay the  man  but when you pay the man  i  i i think i think that is a really  really tough signing mike  yeah i agree with you peter because the  guy has limitations and as we see more  and more mobile quarterbacks and what  you can do when you combine the ability  to throw the ball effectively with the  ability to move around to escape  pressure to extend the play kirk cousins  cannot extend the play the only way he's  effective is if the blocking is holding  back the pass rush which doesn't always  happen every game you can have multiple  occasions where somebody gets through  and you've got to deal with if you're  the quarterback they have the play  actions and the bootlegs that only work  if the running game is firing on all  cylinders it's a very basic offense they  have to replace kevin stefanski my guess  is it's going to be gary kubiak or his  son clint who takes over the offense and  they need a new defensive coordinator  it's apparently possibly maybe going to  be adam zimmer mike's son who's been the  linebackers coach for the last six years  so you know they have some adjustments  to make they have some big decisions  looming and i agree with you on cousins  you don't just pay him because he's due  to be paid or because the markets  continue to grow what does he really  give you he gives you a guy who can win  when you're playing against a lesser  team  but can he win when you're facing a team  with a great defense can he win can he  go point for point with a great  offense like the rams last year when  they weren't able to beat them in a  shootout in la on a thursday night i  just think there's a even though they  beat the saints and you got to give them  credit for that the fact that they lost  so convincingly and could get nothing  going offensively against the 49ers  makes me more inclined to believe that  what we saw last week was not some new  development and some new reality for  kirk cousins it was just you know closer  to an aberration and you'll get those  from time to time but to truly be a  contender you gotta have a quarterback  who can deliver far more often than once  a year in a big spot  hi i'm mike tarico and thanks for  watching make sure to hit subscribe for  the latest news and highlights from nbc  sports
 

